==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|la|factum}}. See {{m|en|fact}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|facta|s}}

# {{lb|en|legal}} Somebody's own [[act]] and [[deed]].
#: {{ux|en|{{w|Fraud in the factum|Fraud in the '''factum'''}}}}
## {{lb|en|legal|civil law}} Anything stated and made certain.
## {{lb|en|legal}} The due [[execution]] of a [[will]], including everything necessary to its [[validity]].
## {{lb|en|legal|Canada}} A [[statement]] of [[fact]] and [[law]] delivered before a [[court]].
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=2009 January 31|author=Isabel Teotonio|title=Police mole trapped teen, court told|journal=Toronto Star|url=http://www.thestar.com/News/GTA/article/580204
|passage=But according to a '''factum''' filed by Crown prosecutors, Shaikh's status was "confidential informer," therefore RCMP did not direct him about what to do at the camp.}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics|obsolete}} A [[product]] {{gloss|result of [[multiply]]ing two numbers}}.

